was a battle. At the end of the battle some rebel Aes Sedai showed themselves as being party to the rescue. But that they didn't follow directions. To their detriment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it. Didn't they come to help him? Shouldn't he be happy there are extra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T19:45:13-07:00","id":1376769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374074-scene-inspiration?p=1376758#post1376758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't get it. Didn't they come to help him? Shouldn't he be happy there are extra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere near that part of the series, but if I'm right this is after a number of colossal eff ups on the part of the Aes Sedai that made things significantly harder and worse than they should have been. (Like there is apparently debate on whether or not the leader at one point had their mind shattered by bad guys to be as incompotent as she was or if she was legitimately that crazy.)<br /> <br /> My main guess is that this is more a response to them ignoring instruction and trying to show how they're in control and don't have to listen. IE if they had actually sent six as instructed then it would have been taken as a sign of being willing to cooperate or help. Instead they sent more establishing they felt they didn't actually need to listen to the requests or instructions of potential allies and from Rand's general opinion on the Aes Sedai from the first few books probably is interpreted as them feeling they don't need to because they're superior to everyone. (Also by this point Rand is probably way crazier from the increasing presence of his predecessesor in his head then he was in earlier books.)<br /> <br /> Basically it isn't finding out you had a bad count of troops among your allies. This is requesting your ally show up for a meeting and strategic discussion and then them insisting on moving a platoon into your home when they show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-26-2020, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T05:41:37-07:00","id":1376802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374074-scene-inspiration?p=1376758#post1376758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't get it. Didn't they come to help him? Shouldn't he be happy there are extra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting it spoilers for those who haven't read it or isn't there yet.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Salidar Aes Sedai did come to help. However, they didn't actually affect the outcome all that much. It was Taim's Asha'man who really affected things. Nalek is also right, Rand essentially fled Caemlyn because he learned that there were now 13 or more Aes Sedai in the city. Which is the amount that can gentle him. He told them to send 6 to Cairhein. They sent 9. It's indicative of how haughty and self-important they view themselves. They ignored instructions. And with how the White Tower Aes Sedai kidnapped him, shielded him, kept him tight in a box and regularly beat him; it was not a good time to be be show disobeying instruction.<br /> <br /> Also, overall the scene is important because up until now, Aes Sedai had never laid fealty at another's feet. They've always been top dog 